---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy Policy — WorkLog" description="How WorkLog handles account, work, client, finance, optional wellness and support information." >
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container narrow"><span class="eyebrow">LEGAL · DRAFT FOR REVIEW</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="page-meta">Last updated October 10, 2026</p><div class="notice-box">This policy is a product-specific draft. The operator’s legal name, governing jurisdiction and final retention/deletion practices must be confirmed before public launch.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section section-space"><article class="container legal-copy">
    <h2>Information you add</h2><p>WorkLog may store your account email and profile details; client and project records; work descriptions, notes and time; invoices, income and expenses; reminders; and, if you choose to use them, profile photos and gym, meal or body-measurement records. Some records can contain information about your clients, so only add information you are permitted to manage.</p>
    <h2>How information is used</h2><p>Information is used to provide the WorkLog features you choose, sync your account, create invoices and reports, send account/security emails, deliver support replies and protect the service. The optional assistant uses allow-listed aggregate metrics for selected suggestions; it is not intended to receive client names, notes or transaction rows.</p>
    <h2>Service providers and storage</h2><p>WorkLog uses Supabase for authentication, database and file storage. Netlify hosts the public website and may process website requests and contact-form delivery. Email providers process account and support messages. These providers handle information under their own terms and security practices. The website does not intentionally sell personal information or use advertising trackers.</p>
    <h2>Invoices shared by link</h2><p>An online invoice link is a private token link, not an identity check. Anyone who receives the link may be able to view the invoice fields displayed on that page. Share links only with the intended recipient and contact support if a link needs attention.</p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can edit profile and work records in the app, export supported data, choose whether to use optional features, and request account deletion through the account controls. Deletion may take time to propagate through backups or provider systems. Support can help with access or privacy questions.</p>
    <h2>Security and retention</h2><p>WorkLog uses account access controls and provider security features, but no online service can promise absolute security. Information is kept while needed to provide the service, meet legitimate operational needs or comply with applicable obligations; final retention periods need to be confirmed by the operator.</p>
    <h2>Children and changes</h2><p>WorkLog is intended for adults managing their own work, not for children. This policy may change as the product changes; the updated date above will be revised when material changes are made.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a class="inline-link" href="mailto:worklog.support@gmail.com">worklog.support@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </article></section>
</SiteLayout>
